 OPS ID but I  prefer to type on the latest version of  the butterfly keyboard backlighting was  also distracting at night with lights  built all around the keys but if you're  coming from a different laptop you'll  likely have the same kind or maybe no  backlighting at all  behind these keys we have hidden  speakers and the volume surprised me  we've been testing different Windows  laptops lately like the 2019 XPS  two-in-one and even though that is over  two thousand dollars once backed out the  speakers are a fair bit quieter than  this old MacBooks  the sound quality was noticeably worse  than a new MacBooks but for usability  when listening to music podcasts or  watching videos the loudspeakers are  surprisingly capable another  surprisingly usable part of the system  is the i/o which actually I guess isn't  too surprising all of the new Macs use  only USB type-c which works fine for me  most of the time and I'd have to use  dongles too often but for somebody that  edits photos and videos all the time  having that SD card slot is just so nice  we also have two USB type 8 ports and a  single Thunderbolt 2 port which is  enough for most people now if you don't  need that SD card slot it can be easily  used to cheaply expand the internal SSD  with these flush-mount SD cards these  aren't super fast but they'll do a good  job for photos videos and other files if  you're like me and have a MacBook Air  that has 128 gigs of SSD space this is  something that you can't really pull off  well with the new MacBook and another  thing a new MacBook can't do is to be  able to swap out the SSD after you buy  it since everything is soldered in the  stock 128 gigabyte SSD is surprisingly  fast but if you really want to get  serious with your storage you can  actually upgrade to a larger and faster  nvme SSD drive to speed things up not  many people know that up from 2015 which  is my model and on they actually had a  4x m2 slot you just need a little cheap  adapter to be able t